training split only) is the negative control; rephrase is leakage of the paraphrased test.
A methodological caution underlies the base-referencing. The raw
original-minus-paraphrase gap is contaminated by a benchmark-level difficulty shift: on HellaSwag,
clean base models show a raw gap near +0.21, as large as deliberately contaminated models,
because paraphrasing HellaSwag’s adversarial endings makes the items harder for everyone.
Referencing each model to a clean baseline removes this shift; without it, the audit would report
widespread false contamination on HellaSwag.
