3.3 DIF Analysis
DIF effects are consistently strong across both
benchmarks (Figure 11). On MGSM, an average
of 48.3% of tested items (range: 34–63% across 10
languages) show significant DIF relative to English,
with a mean anchor-corrected shift of |∆b| = 1.14
logits. On MMLU, 31.8% of items show signif-
icant DIF on average (range: 21–69% across 6
focal languages), with a mean shift of |∆b| = 1.50
logits. Pooled across both benchmarks, this cor-
responds to an average shift in probability of a
correct response of roughly 22 percentage points
at the item’s own difficulty level, rising to roughly
38 points among items flagged as DIF. Swahili
